    { q: 'A silicon crystal doped with 10¹⁶ donors per cm³ (one atom in ~5 million) conducts about…', choices: ['unchanged', 'hundreds of thousands of times better than intrinsic silicon', '10¹⁶ times worse', 'not at all'], answer: 1, why: 'Intrinsic nᵢ ≈ 10¹⁰ cm⁻³; doping sets n = 10¹⁶ — a millionfold carrier increase, turning ~230,000 Ω·cm material into ~0.5 Ω·cm. Trace impurity, astronomical effect: that is why fabs demand nine-nines purity.' },
